# Hash-pinned evidence. `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout converts
# these to CRLF, which changes their byte content without changing their git
# diff (autocrlf normalizes the comparison), so the corruption is invisible to
# `git status` while breaking every sha256 pin computed against the committed
# LF bytes. Found 2026-08-05 when `exhibition/current/external_metrics/source_
# data/dicos-p9/epoch_0038/{auroc,four_momentum}/metrics.json` failed
# `load_transactions()`'s hash check with an exact CRLF-sized byte delta.
# Forcing LF for these trees makes every future checkout match the pin it was
# committed against, on any OS.
exhibition/**/*.json text eol=lf
audit/**/*.json text eol=lf
configs/**/*.json text eol=lf
prep/**/*.json text eol=lf
